Patch-Source: https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-php/pull/193
From: Andy Postnikov <apostnikov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] keep zend_object last in php_msgpack_base_t

zend_object must be the last member of a custom object struct: its
trailing properties_table[1] is sized by zend_object_properties_size(),
which is -sizeof(zval) for a class without declared properties, so
php_msgpack_base_new() allocates less than sizeof(php_msgpack_base_t).

force_f32 sat after the embedded zend_object and therefore outside the
allocation. On armhf/armv7, where zval is 8-byte aligned, the store in
MessagePack::__construct() lands in the next ZendMM slot of the same bin
and clobbers whatever lives there, e.g. a packed array's u.v.flags,
which later crashes msgpack_serialize_array().
---
 msgpack_class.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/msgpack_class.c b/msgpack_class.c
--- a/msgpack_class.c
+++ b/msgpack_class.c
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@
 typedef struct {
     long php_only;
     zend_bool assoc;
-    zend_object object;
     zend_bool force_f32;
+    zend_object object;
 } php_msgpack_base_t;

 typedef struct {
